ostilities against the Islamic Republic of Iran that have not been authorized by Congress.","question":"On the Motion to Discharge","result":"Motion to Discharge Rejected","counts":{"yeas":"47","nays":"53","present":"","absent":""},"source":"https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00328.htm","parties":{"D":{"Y":44,"N":1,"NV":0},"R":{"Y":1,"N":50,"NV":0},"I":{"Y":2,"N":0,"NV":0}},"positions":{"G000386":"N","M000133":"Y","S000148":"Y","W000779":"Y","M000355":"N","D000563":"Y","B001236":"N","S001150":"Y","C001047":"N","V000128":"Y","B001243":"N","M001169":"Y","H001042":"Y","G000555":"Y","W000800":"Y","C001075":"N","P000595":"Y","H001046":"Y","L000570":"Y","L000571":"N","Y000064":"N","L000575":"N","S001184":"N","C001095":"N","D000622":"Y","D000618":"N","C001096":"N","G000574":"Y","B001299":"N","B001303":"Y","B001305":"N","M001198":"N","R000608":"Y","C001114":"N","K000394":"Y","S001208":"Y","R000122":"Y","S000033":"Y","C000880":"N","W000437":"N","M000934":"N","T000250":"N","B001230":"Y","C000127":"Y","M001153":"N","C001056":"N","K000367":"Y","W000802":"Y","B001261":"N","R000584":"N","S001181":"Y","M001176":"Y","W000805":"Y","B001267":"Y","C001088":"Y","B001277":"Y","P000603":"Y","H001061":"N","L000577":"N","J000293":"N","S001194":"Y","K000383":"Y","W000817":"Y","F000463":"N","C001098":"N","K000384":"Y","B001288":"Y","S001198":"N","E000295":"N","T000476":"N","R000605":"N","C001113":"Y","H001076":"Y","K000393":"N","S001203":"Y","H001079":"N","H001089":"N","S001217":"N","K000377":"Y","H000601":"N","H000273":"Y","T000278":"N","O000174":"Y","P000145":"Y","W000790":"Y","B001319":"N","F000479":"N","R000618":"N","S001227":"N","A000382":"Y","M001243":"N","M001242":"N","S001232":"N","J000312":"N","H001104":"N","M001244":"N","M001111":"Y","C001035":"N"}}],"bills":[],"promises":[{"kind":"promise","id":"p-C001088-001","bioguide":"C001088","name":"Christopher A. Coons","party":"Democrat","state":"DE","quote":"Mr. President, I rise to follow the comments of my colleague from the Commonwealth of Virginia, and I intend to join him in voting against any proceedings by the United States military, any action by our President to invade or occupy Cuba without authorization by the Senate, by the House, by the Congress of the United States.","promise":"Said he intends to vote against U.S. military action to invade or occupy Cuba without congressional authorization.","status":"kept","verified":false,"source_url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/crec/2026/04/28/172/74/modified/CREC-2026-04-28-pt1-PgS2066-2.htm","source_date":"2026-04-28","platform":null},{"kind":"promise","id":"p-C001088-002","bioguide":"C001088","name":"Christopher A. Coons","party":"Democrat","state":"DE","quote":"So as the question of how we will conduct ourselves going forward in Cuba, in Ukraine, in the Middle East is before this body, I intend to continue to vote for the Congress to take its constitutional role and, more than anything, for us to not hand away the power of the purse to an overreaching President.","promise":"Said he intends to keep voting to assert Congress's constitutional role and power of the purse.","status":"not_started","verified":false,"source_url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/crec/2026/04/28/172/74/modified/CREC-2026-04-28-pt1-PgS2066-2.htm","source_date":"2026-04-28","platform":null},{"kind":"promise","id":"p-M001176-001","bioguide":"M001176","name":"Jeff Merkley","party":"Democrat","state":"OR","quote":"Today, the Senate votes on war powers resolutions to rein in Trump\u2019s illegal war with Iran.\n \nI will vote YES\u2014as I have repeatedly. I encourage my Republican colleagues to join me. We know this is wrong\u2014it\u2019s not a partisan issue.","promise":"Said he will vote yes on war powers resolutions to rein in Trump's war with Iran.","status":"kept","verified":false,"source_url":"https://x.com/SenJeffMerkley/status/2044479841093787650","source_date":"2026-04-15","platform":null},{"kind":"promise","id":"p-L000571-001","bioguide":"L000571","name":"Cynthia M. Lummis","party":"Republican","state":"WY","quote":"President Trump\u2019s objective is clear: Iran cannot have a nuclear weapon.\n\nI will vote to support @POTUS and give him all the tools available to defend America\u2019s interests.","promise":"Said she will vote to support the President and give him tools to defend America\u2019s interests regarding Iran.","status":"kept","verified":false,"source_url":"https://x.com/SenLummis/status/2029288520217420237","source_date":"2026-03-04","platform":null}],"statements":[{"kind":"statement","id":"s-B001288-007","bioguide":"B001288","name":"Cory A. Booker","party":"Democrat","state":"NJ","quote":"This is the sixth time that a group of us has said every single week we are going to continue to bring these War Powers Resolutions to the floor.","promise":null,"status":null,"verified":false,"source_url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/crec/2026/04/30/172/76/modified/CREC-2026-04-30-pt1-PgS2152.htm","source_date":"2026-04-30","platform":"floor speech"},{"kind":"statement","id":"s-M001176-001","bioguide":"M001176","name":"Jeff Merkley","party":"Democrat","state":"OR","quote":"I just introduced a War Powers Resolution to rein in Trump\u2019s illegal war with Iran.\n \nDemocrats are sending a clear message: we\u2019re going to keep voting on these resolutions until they pass.\n \nRepublicans need to fulfill their oath to the Constitution and vote YES.","promise":null,"status":null,"verified":false,"source_url":"https://x.com/SenJeffMerkley/status/2043844538494533692","source_date":"2026-04-14","platform":"X"},{"kind":"statement","id":"s-M000355-006","bioguide":"M000355","name":"Mitch McConnell","party":"Republican","state":"KY","quote":"Therefore, I will oppose the [Kaine war powers resolution on Iran] and would recommend our colleagues do the same.","promise":null,"status":null,"verified":false,"source_url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/crec/2026/03/04/172/41/modified/CREC-2026-03-04-pt1-PgS773.htm","source_date":"2026-03-04","platform":"floor speech"},{"kind":"statement","id":"s-R000122-003","bioguide":"R000122","name":"Jack Reed","party":"Democrat","state":"RI","quote":"Mr. President, last week, this body advanced a War Powers Resolution to rein in President Trump's unauthorized military actions in Venezuela.","promise":null,"status":null,"verified":false,"source_url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/crec/2026/01/14/172/10/modified/CREC-2026-01-14-pt1-PgS186-2.htm","source_date":"2026-01-14","platform":"floor speech"}]}